  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Derivation of the scaling-region ODE\nInsert $q(u)=q_{hw}(u)\\,p(\\phi u)$, set $v=\\phi u$, and expand Baxter divided by $u^L q_{hw}(u) p(v)$ in $\\phi$ at fixed $v$. Only large-$u$ data enter: $\\Delta_\\pm/u^L = 1 \\pm iS/u+\\dots$ with $S=\\sum_a s_a$, and $q_{hw}(u\\pm i)/q_{hw}(u) = 1\\pm iK/u+\\dots$ with $K=M_{hw}$. $T$ is written $2\\cos\\phi\\,u^2+\\phi\\,\\tau_1 u+t_0$. Order $\\phi^0$ and $\\phi^1$ vanish identically; order $\\phi^2$ gives the ODE.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* generic large-u data: Delta_pm = u^2 + (-Th \\[PlusMinus] I S)u + d_pm ; q_hw = u^K(1 + b1/u + b2/u^2) ; p generic function of v = phi u.\n   T = 2cos(phi) u^2 + (-2Th + phi tau1) u + t0 : the O(phi^0) part of t1 is forced by the order-phi equation *)\nClear[pp, v, f, Th, S, K, dP, dM, b1, b2, tau1, t0, u];\nqR[s_] := (1 + s I/u)^K (1 + b1/(u + s I) + b2/(u + s I)^2)/(1 + b1/u + b2/u^2);\nres = (2 Cos[f] u^2 + (-2 Th + f tau1) u + t0)/u^2 - ((u^2 + (-Th + I S) u + dP)/u^2 Exp[I f] qR[1] pp[v + I f] + (u^2 + (-Th - I S) u + dM)/u^2 Exp[-I f] qR[-1] pp[v - I f])/pp[v];\nord = Normal[Series[res /. u -> v/f, {f, 0, 2}]];\nlowOrders = Simplify[{Coefficient[ord, f, 0], Coefficient[ord, f, 1]}];\node = Collect[Simplify[-Coefficient[ord, f, 2] v pp[v]], {pp[v], pp'[v], pp''[v]}, Simplify];\n(* polynomial p of degree m: regularity at v=0 fixes t0, leading power fixes tau1 = -2(S+K+m) ; then x=-2v gives Laguerre with alpha = 2(S+K)-1 *)\nlagCheck = Simplify[ode /. {t0 -> dM + dP + K - K^2 - 2 K S, tau1 -> -2 (S + K + m)} /. pp -> Function[w, LaguerreL[m, 2 (S + K) - 1, -2 w]] /. m -> 3];\nGrid[{{\"orders phi^0, phi^1\", lowOrders}, {\"order phi^2 (\\[Times] v p)\", ode}, {\"Laguerre check, m=3, generic S,K\", lagCheck}}, Frame -> All]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
